  "notes": "{堪|こら}える emphasizes internal fortitude and self-control.\n\nKANJI NOTE:\nAlternatively written as {耐|こら}える, though {堪|こら}える is more common. Both share the sense of endurance.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みを{堪|こら}える: to endure pain\n- {涙|なみだ}を{堪|こら}える: to hold back tears\n- {笑|わら}いを{堪|こら}える: to suppress laughter\n- {空腹|くうふく}を{堪|こら}える: to endure hunger\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {耐|た}える: to endure, withstand (more formal)\n- {我慢|がまん}する: to be patient, put up with",
